# AI Interview Guide Backend

## Setup

1. Clone the repo:

```bash
git clone https://github.com/yourusername/ai-interview-guide.git
cd ai-interview-guide/backend
Create a .env file from the example:
cp .env.example .env


Fill in your values for API keys, JWT secret, etc.

Run with Docker Compose:

docker-compose up --build


Your backend will be accessible at http://localhost:5000 and connect automatically to the MongoDB container.


---

## ✅ Key Points

- Others can **clone and run your project** without needing your real secrets.  
- Docker will **build the image locally** from your Dockerfile.  
- You **don’t need to push images to Docker Hub** unless you want pre-built images.  

